          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.96,
          "end": 67.923,
          "en": "on that signal like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 69.81,
          "end": 73.23,
          "en": "Or of course, we could rely on this input binding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 73.23,
          "end": 75.45,
          "en": "to keep things even simpler.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 75.45,
          "end": 77.46000000000001,
          "en": "But here for demo purposes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 77.46000000000001,
          "end": 78.739,
          "en": "I'll use this approach.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.739,
          "end": 82.02,
          "en": "And then in the tasks component, HTML file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.02,
          "end": 84.316,
          "en": "we of course wanna reorder again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 84.316,
          "end": 86.943,
          "en": "since it is now a signal again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.65,
          "end": 90.78,
          "en": "But in the TypeScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 90.78,
          "end": 95.4,
          "en": "we now need to edit this computed signal function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.4,
          "end": 97.28999999999999,
          "en": "because now it's no longer enough",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.28999999999999,
          "end": 101.97,
          "en": "to just filter our signals and get a filtered array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 101.97,
          "end": 105.36,
          "en": "Instead, that filtered array now also must",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 105.36,
          "end": 108.024,
          "en": "be sorted with the sort method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 108.024,
          "end": 111.99000000000001,
          "en": "And this sort method is of course a default method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 111.99000000000001,
          "end": 114.688,
          "en": "offered by JavaScript in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 114.688,
          "end": 117.143,
          "en": "It takes a function as an argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 117.143,
          "end": 121.92,
          "en": "a function which will itself receive two parameters,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 121.92,
          "end": 124.17,
          "en": "since it will always compare two items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 124.17,
          "end": 126.145,
          "en": "from that array at the same time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.145,
          "end": 128.76,
          "en": "And in this function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 128.76,
          "end": 131.137,
          "en": "I then want to take a look at my order",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 131.137,
          "end": 134.445,
          "en": "and check if it's DESC for descending.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 134.445,
          "end": 135.762,
          "en": "And in that case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 135.762,
          "end": 140.762,
          "en": "I'll return the result of comparing A's ID to B'S ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 141,
          "end": 143.85,
          "en": "And if it's greater, I wanna return minus one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 143.85,
          "end": 145.63400000000001,
          "en": "otherwise plus one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 145.63400000000001,
          "end": 150.63400000000001,
          "en": "Else if order is ascending or not set,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.1,
          "end": 154.017,
          "en": "I'll return the opposite,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 154.017,
          "end": 158.073,
          "en": "and that should give me the sorting behavior I want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.35,
          "end": 163.41,
          "en": "And if you do that all, and you go back,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.41,
          "end": 166.058,
          "en": "you should see tasks in this order.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 166.058,
          "end": 170.57999999999998,
          "en": "So here, the task with the title of prepare issue template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 170.57999999999998,
          "end": 173.37,
          "en": "comes first and that makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 173.37,
          "end": 175.736,
          "en": "because it has an ID that's bigger than",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.736,
          "end": 180.123,
          "en": "the ID of this build first prototype task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 181.41,
          "end": 184.68,
          "en": "And since the default is to sort in descending order,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 184.68,
          "end": 186.78,
          "en": "the bigger ID should come first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 186.78,
          "end": 188.606,
          "en": "and that's exactly what's happening here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 188.606,
          "end": 191.67,
          "en": "But as I then click sort ascending,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 191.67,
          "end": 194.1,
          "en": "the order changes and the item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 194.1,
          "end": 196.77,
          "en": "with the smaller ID comes first.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.77,
          "end": 199.23,
          "en": "And now we can toggle between these modes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 199.23,
          "end": 203.25,
          "en": "with help of query parameters and in this case signals.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 203.25,
          "end": 207.51,
          "en": "And that's of course, just one way of implementing this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.51,
          "end": 211.14,
          "en": "Not necessarily the shortest and most concise way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 211.14,
          "end": 215.373,
          "en": "but hopefully a way where it's clear what's going on here.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
